    "notes": "Baroque stage seating: violins antiphonal left/right, cello and bass center-right, harpsichord center-rear. El telar is the only moving source: it holds far overhead until bar 25, approaches, circles the listener through the dissolution and stretto (directly behind at the stretto downbeat), retreats for the echo, then WEAVES left-right like a shuttle through the hemiola before settling overhead for the coda. La sierra sits below the floor.",
